import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbe/assbes.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code='ASSBEs'
  standardType='ASBE'
  title='Accounting Standards for Small Business Enterprises (ASSBEs) â€” Framework Overview'
  description='The Accounting Standards for Small Business Enterprises (ASSBEs) provide a simplified framework for small business enterprises in China, reducing the complexity of full ASBE standards while maintaining core accounting principles.'
  issued='2004-01'
  latestAmendment='2017-01'
  status='Active'
  summary='ASSBEs are the simplified accounting standards for small business enterprises in China.'
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope â€” Small Enterprises Without Public Accountability" },
        { id: "s3", label: "Why a Separate Framework Exists" },
        { id: "s4", label: "THE KEY SIMPLIFICATION â€” No Deferred Tax Accounting" },
        { id: "s5", label: "Predominantly Historical Cost â€” No Fair Value Elections" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Simplified Financial Instruments Treatment" },
        { id: "s7", label: "No Consolidation, Hedge Accounting, or Complex Group Reporting" },
        { id: "s8", label: "No EPS, Segment Reporting, or Comparable Public-Company Disclosures" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Worked Example â€” Current Tax Only, No Deferred Tax Asset" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Worked Example â€” Historical Cost Investment Property Under ASSBEs" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s13", label: "Relationship to IFRS for SMEs" },
        { id: "s14", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s16", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
<div class="callout info" style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto 20px;text-align:center;">FRAMEWORK NOTE: ASSBEs are not part of the main numbered ASBE series (1â€“41) â€” they are a wholly separate, simplified accounting framework issued by China's Ministry of Finance for qualifying small enterprises. Most listed and larger companies apply full ASBE instead; the specific size thresholds qualifying an enterprise for ASSBEs should be confirmed against current MOF guidance.</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A reduced-complexity framework for smaller enterprises</div><div class="principle">ASSBEs are a SEPARATE, SIMPLIFIED accounting FRAMEWORK issued by China'S Ministry of FINANCE for QUALIFYING small ENTERPRISES â€” REDUCING the RECOGNITION, measurement, and DISCLOSURE complexity of FULL ASBE, WHILE retaining a BASIC level of FINANCIAL reporting USEFULNESS. THIS framework PLAYS a ROLE broadly PARALLEL to the IASB'S OWN "IFRS for SMEs" standard internationally.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope â€” Small Enterprises Without Public Accountability</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Non-listed enterprises meeting specified size criteria</div><div class="principle">ASSBEs apply to SMALL enterprises MEETING SPECIFIED size CRITERIA (GENERALLY based on THRESHOLDS such as TOTAL assets, ANNUAL revenue, and EMPLOYEE headcount), that are NOT listed or PUBLICLY traded, and that DO NOT have PUBLIC accountability â€” MOST listed COMPANIES and LARGER enterprises INSTEAD apply the FULL ASBE framework COVERED throughout the REST of this poster series.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Why a Separate Framework Exists</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Balancing information usefulness against compliance burden</div><div class="principle">FULL ASBE â€” WITH its DETAILED recognition, MEASUREMENT, and DISCLOSURE requirements ACROSS 41+ specific STANDARDS â€” represents a GENUINELY SUBSTANTIAL compliance BURDEN, PARTICULARLY for SMALL enterprises WITHOUT dedicated, SOPHISTICATED accounting FUNCTIONS. ASSBEs REDUCE this burden BY simplifying or ELIMINATING requirements that ARE of LIMITED practical VALUE for smaller, NON-public enterprises â€” WHILE STILL providing a COHERENT, useful BASIS of financial REPORTING for SMALL business STAKEHOLDERS (banks, TAX authorities, and OWNERS).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>THE KEY SIMPLIFICATION â€” No Deferred Tax Accounting</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A return to the tax payable method</div><div class="principle">UNLIKE FULL ASBE (WHICH requires the BALANCE sheet LIABILITY method for DEFERRED tax UNDER ASBE No. 18 â€” see the COMPANION poster), ASSBEs GENERALLY apply the SIMPLER "TAX PAYABLE method" â€” RECOGNISING ONLY current TAX expense, WITH NO deferred TAX assets or LIABILITIES recognised AT ALL. THIS is a GENUINELY significant SIMPLIFICATION, AVOIDING the SUBSTANTIAL complexity of TEMPORARY difference tracking and DEFERRED tax CALCULATIONS that SMALL enterprises would OTHERWISE face.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Predominantly Historical Cost â€” No Fair Value Elections</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Simplifying an already-cautious full-ASBE default even further</div><div class="principle">ASSBEs are BUILT almost ENTIRELY around HISTORICAL cost MEASUREMENT â€” WITHOUT the NARROW fair VALUE elections FULL ASBE permits for INVESTMENT property (ASBE No. 3) or BIOLOGICAL assets (ASBE No. 5) in LIMITED circumstances. GIVEN full ASBE ITSELF already RESTRICTS fair VALUE measurement HEAVILY relative to IFRS (see the COMPANION posters), ASSBEs REPRESENT an EVEN FURTHER simplification, ELIMINATING fair VALUE measurement ENTIRELY for THESE asset categories.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Simplified Financial Instruments Treatment</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">No expected credit loss model, no complex classification</div><div class="principle">ASSBEs do NOT apply the FULL classification and EXPECTED credit LOSS framework introduced UNDER ASBE No. 22 (see the COMPANION poster) â€” FINANCIAL instruments are GENERALLY measured at AMORTISED cost or COST, WITHOUT the SOPHISTICATED business-MODEL and SPPI-based CLASSIFICATION testing, or the FORWARD-looking impairment MODEL, full ASBE REQUIRES.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>No Consolidation, Hedge Accounting, or Complex Group Reporting</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Reflecting the typically simpler ownership structure of small enterprises</div><div class="principle">GIVEN small ENTERPRISES typically LACK complex GROUP structures, ASSBEs DO NOT include a CONSOLIDATED financial STATEMENTS requirement PARALLELING ASBE No. 33, and DO NOT include HEDGE accounting PROVISIONS paralleling ASBE No. 24 â€” SIMPLIFICATIONS reflecting the GENUINELY different PRACTICAL circumstances of the SMALL enterprises this framework TARGETS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>No EPS, Segment Reporting, or Comparable Public-Company Disclosures</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Disclosures tailored to a non-public user base</div><div class="principle">SINCE ASSBEs APPLY only to NON-listed enterprises, THERE is NO requirement PARALLELING ASBE No. 34 (EARNINGS Per Share) or ASBE No. 35 (SEGMENT Reporting) â€” DISCLOSURES genuinely GEARED toward PUBLIC capital MARKETS users, WITH LIMITED relevance to a SMALL enterprise'S typically NARROWER stakeholder BASE (owners, BANKS, tax AUTHORITIES).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example â€” Current Tax Only, No Deferred Tax Asset</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Simplified tax accounting under ASSBEs</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A warranty provision under the tax payable method</div><div class="wk-body">A small enterprise recognises a RMB 500,000 warranty provision, which is not yet tax-deductible until the warranty costs are actually paid.</div><div class="wk-answer">UNDER ASSBEs, the ENTERPRISE recognises ONLY its CURRENT tax LIABILITY BASED on TAXABLE profit â€” NO deferred TAX asset is RECOGNISED for the RMB 500,000 provision'S FUTURE tax DEDUCTIBILITY, UNLIKE the SAME transaction UNDER full ASBE No. 18 (see the COMPANION poster, WHERE a DEFERRED tax asset WOULD be recognised).</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example â€” Historical Cost Investment Property Under ASSBEs</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">No fair value option available at all</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A small enterprise's rental property</div><div class="wk-body">A small enterprise holds a leased-out commercial unit with a cost of RMB 3,000,000 and a 30-year useful life, located in a market with genuinely active, reliable price evidence.</div><div class="wk-answer">DESPITE the ACTIVE market EVIDENCE that MIGHT have QUALIFIED the property for the FAIR VALUE model UNDER full ASBE No. 3 (see the COMPANION poster), UNDER ASSBEs the ENTERPRISE MUST apply the COST model, DEPRECIATING RMB 3,000,000 Ã· 30 = <strong>RMB 100,000 per year</strong> â€” the FAIR value OPTION IS simply NOT available AT ALL under THIS simplified FRAMEWORK.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A reduced, but still coherent, disclosure package</div><div class="check-list"><span>A Balance Sheet, Income Statement, and (in a simplified format) a Cash Flow Statement</span><span>Basic accounting policies applied</span><span>Significant transactions and balances relevant to a small enterprise's stakeholders</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether an enterprise genuinely qualifies for ASSBEs, based on the applicable size thresholds</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Generally reduced relative to full ASBE, given the elimination of fair value and deferred tax estimation</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS for SMEs</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison â€” ASSBEs vs IFRS for SMEs</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASSBEs</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS for SMEs</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Policy rationale</span><span>Reduced complexity for small, non-public enterprises</span><span>Reduced complexity for small, non-public enterprises â€” same rationale</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Deferred tax</span><span>NOT required â€” tax payable method</span><span>REQUIRED â€” a simplified deferred tax model still applies</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">ASSBEs GO genuinely FURTHER than IFRS for SMEs in SOME respects â€” MOST notably, ELIMINATING deferred tax ACCOUNTING entirely, WHERE IFRS for SMEs RETAINS a (simplified) DEFERRED tax requirement.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">The simplified statement set</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Current tax expense</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">IS</span></span><span>No deferred tax component recognised</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 18</span><span>Income Taxes â€” the full deferred tax framework ASSBEs simplify away from entirely</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 3 / No. 22</span><span>Investment Property / Financial Instruments â€” supply the fair value and classification frameworks ASSBEs simplify or eliminate</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Tax payable method</div><div class="glossary-def">A simplified tax accounting approach recognising only current tax expense, with no deferred tax assets or liabilities, used under ASSBEs.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Public accountability</div><div class="glossary-def">A characteristic of entities whose debt or equity trades in a public market, or that hold assets in a fiduciary capacity for a broad group of outsiders, disqualifying them from simplified small-enterprise frameworks.</div></div>
</div>
</div>
    <FinancialStatementKey />

  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.assbes || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>

